From e276c0ee3db602af801c02c4e6fd1fe7ad28e65a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:27:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: hear only the connected client on the tracking and
 control sockets

Both UDP sockets are bound on every interface, so any host that could reach
the Mac could send head pose and controller input (9945), keep a vanished
client alive (the liveness watchdog counts tracking packets), or end the
session with a one-byte ServerDisconnect (9946).

While a Wi-Fi client is connected, only its address is heard there now;
with none, tracking is ignored and control is limited to discovery and
ClientConnect, which client admission already rules on. The port is not
compared: a restarted client returns on a new port from the same host.
Foreign datagrams are counted and logged (first five, then every 1000).
OXRSYS_ACCEPT_ANY_SOURCE=1 restores the old behaviour.

This stops a stranger on the network, not one who can forge the client's
source address on the same link; that needs a shared key.
